  "reason": "The existing evidence shows config_013 (accuracy 0.6352) is the best so far, but it uses PCA RNA and avgpool aggregation. Config_015 tests scGPT RNA (potentially more expressive) with transformer aggregation (which may capture complex interactions better than avgpool), while maintaining weighted fusion (proven effective in config_005/config_013). This balances exploration of RNA encoder improvements with the promising aggregation method. Expected cost is ~8.5 GPU hours (higher than config_013's 7.02 due to scGPT and transformer), but the potential accuracy gain justifies the cost given the current budget."
